.TH ZDOT 1 "2026-11" "zdot" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zdot \- explicit dotfile deployment and Git synchronization
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zdot
init --root REPO
.br
.B zdot
plan|apply|status|remove --root REPO [--target HOME] [--profile FILE]
.br
.B zdot
sync --root REPO status|pull|push
.SH DESCRIPTION
zdot maps files and directories from a repository into a target using symbolic
links. Profiles contain source and destination separated by one tab. Both
paths are relative. Blank lines and comments beginning with # are ignored.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --root PATH
Repository directory. Default is the current directory.
.TP
.B --target PATH
Existing target directory. Default is HOME.
.TP
.B --profile FILE
Repository-relative profile. Default is profile.zdot.
.TP
.B --state-dir PATH
Absolute private recovery directory. Defaults to TARGET/.zdot-state.
Pass the same path for plan, apply, status and remove. Plan and status never
create directories. Apply creates missing state directories with mode 0700.
The path must not overlap the repository or any managed source or destination.
Backups use atomic moves and require the same filesystem as the original files.
.TP
.B --backup
Explicitly preserve conflicting destinations before linking. Valid for apply
and plan. Backups are restored during remove.
.TP
.B --json
Emit versioned JSON for plan, status or mutation results.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init
Create the repository directory, files directory and sample profile. Does not
initialize Git or replace an existing profile.
.TP
.B plan
Inspect every mapping without modifying the filesystem.
.TP
.B apply
Deploy mappings. Reapplication keeps matching links. Conflicts are refused
unless --backup is supplied.
.TP
.B status
Inspect mappings, returning 3 when any destination is missing or conflicting.
.TP
.B remove
Use the saved deployment profile to remove owned links and restore originals.
A replaced destination prevents removal of the entire deployment.
.TP
.B sync
Execute system Git status, pull --ff-only, or push with literal arguments.
No commit, remote, merge strategy or credential is chosen automatically.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I TARGET/.zdot-state
Deployment ownership, saved profiles and preserved originals.
.TP
.I TARGET/.zdot.lock
Legacy target-wide cooperative lock file, retained in default mode.
With --state-dir, a target directory lock avoids creating this file; an existing
legacy lock is also honored. No background process is started.
.SH LIMITS
Linux x86_64 or aarch64, kernel 4.11 or later, and /proc.
Profiles are limited to 128 mappings and 65536 bytes.
Parent traversal, symlink parents and symlink sources are rejected.
Concurrent external mutation is outside the cooperative transaction model.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 for success; 2 for input or filesystem failure; 3 for nonmatching status.
The sync command preserves Git's exit status.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1),
.BR symlink (7)
